{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Anti-inflammatory, anti-sepsis", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "APD analysis reveals that the sequence of this peptide most resembles (47.5% similarity) Cecropin C. Potently active against Gram- E. coli ATCC 25922, including clinical strains, P. aeruginosa ATCC 9027, S. typhimurium ATCC 14028, A. baumannii ATCC 17978 (MIC 0.87-2.33 uM), and Gram+ S. aureus ATCC 6538, B. subtilis ATCC 6633, and M. luteus ATCC 4698 (MIC 14.5-43.7 uM). The peptide is induced in the salivary glands after treatment with E. coli. Like other cecropins, it is helical (0.2 mg/ml) in the presence of SDS (5-40 mM) or LPS (400 ng/ml), very likely membrane targeting. In addtion, SibaCec substantially inhibited NO, TNF-alpha, IL-1beta, and IL-6. It appears that SibaCec exerts its anti-inflammatory effect through inhibition of MAPKs and NF-kB inflammatory signaling pathways.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "26497304", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Parasit Vectors. 2015 Oct 24;8(1):561. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP02621", "source_id": "AP02621", "source_numeric_id": "02621", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP02621", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "A cecropin-like antimicrobial peptide with anti-inflammatory activity from the black fly salivary glands", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
